    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The full-stack change is complete and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented client tracking (add a client with name + email, list all clients) as a small, additive full-stack change:\n\n**Database** (`src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__clients.sql`)\n- New Flyway migration creating a `clients` table (`id` IDENTITY, `name`, `email`).\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST on the Spring Boot host)\n- `Client` record + `NewClient` request DTO.\n- `ClientRepository` \u2014 `JdbcTemplate` data access (`findAll` ordered by id; `create` returning the generated id).\n- Two additive endpoints, one YAML + one logic class each: `GET /api/clients` (`ClientsGetLogic`) and `POST /api/clients` (`ClientsPostLogic`), placed under `rest/api/` so they bypass the SPA fallback.\n- Extended `TestSupportController`: `reset` now `TRUNCATE TABLE clients RESTART IDENTITY`; `seed` inserts client rows with the fixture's explicit ids via `JdbcTemplate` (per the CLAUDE.md rule).\n\n**Front-end** (React)\n- Built the additive routing mechanism the skeleton `router/routes.ts` had as a TODO: features self-register by dropping a `route.tsx`, auto-discovered via `import.meta.glob` \u2014 so adding the feature was a new file, not an edit to the router.\n- Wired the base shell (`main.tsx`) to render nav buttons (`nav-clients`) and the active page \u2014 no per-feature branching.\n- New `features/clients/` feature (`ClientsPage.tsx` + `route.tsx`) with the form (`client-form-name`, `client-form-email`, `client-form-submit`), the `clients-empty` state, and the `clients-table` with `client-row-<id>` / `client-name` / `client-email` cells.\n\nAll `data-testid` anchors match the spec exactly, and both `@core` tests pass. No audit records were required by the request or the spec, so none were added.",
